WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.105
Finishing the task is only part of the

00:00:03.105 --> 00:00:05.861
job. Keep who did it, what changed, and

00:00:05.861 --> 00:00:07.927
the record of the outcome together.

00:00:08.327 --> 00:00:11.591
Start in the queue. Find an available item,

00:00:11.591 --> 00:00:14.854
open its detail, and read the source before

00:00:14.854 --> 00:00:15.670
taking ownership.

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:19.018
Claim the item so the team can see

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:21.966
who is working it. If someone already owns

00:00:21.966 --> 00:00:24.177
it, resolve that handoff before proceeding.

00:00:24.577 --> 00:00:27.995
As the work moves, update its state and

00:00:27.995 --> 00:00:31.413
preserve useful context. Someone opening it later should

00:00:31.413 --> 00:00:34.831
understand what happened and what still needs attention.

00:00:35.231 --> 00:00:38.605
When the work is complete, record the outcome

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:41.978
accurately. Check the amount and action type, then

00:00:41.978 --> 00:00:45.352
inspect the activity connected to the completed item.

00:00:45.752 --> 00:00:48.379
The queue shows the work is finished, and

00:00:48.379 --> 00:00:51.005
the record keeps the outcome. That is the

00:00:51.005 --> 00:00:52.647
loop you want to close.
